    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28">

                <pb facs="0115" n="23" xml:id="pg23"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister
                        Churchill</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d28-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hyde
                                Park</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-26"
                            >August 26, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">From: The President</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To: Colonel Warden, Personal and Secret</p>
                <p>Number 347. I hope you have seen Uncle Joe’s new message which is greatly
                    improved in its tone. As you and he know, I am lost until Monday<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d28-f2"/> and I would let a few days go by till we answer him.</p>
                <p>However, my first feeling is that he has come around to our secondary meeting and
                    that it should be held very soon.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d28-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d28-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the White House Map Room and the British Admiralty Delegation at
                    Washington. Churchill was in Canada at this time.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d28-f2" n="2" xml:id="d28-f2-content">
                <p>August 30, 1943.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
